From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:27:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: stay down after host sleep link loss

When the PCIe link does not come back after system sleep, the host
bridge refuses configuration access to the device or marks it
disconnected. brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3() then went on to access the BARs,
which can stall the CPU. Return -ENODEV and keep the bus down instead;
firmware commands and transmits are then refused early. A later
suspend has nothing to tell such a device either.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #117, commit 40a8b18d. The test is
 pci_device_is_present(), which also covers a device whose port is down
 without being marked disconnected, and the suspend side got the same
 test.]
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c    | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index d7c6a402f..c103f618e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2663,6 +2663,10 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3(struct device *dev)
 	bus = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	devinfo = bus->bus_priv.pcie->devinfo;
 
+	/* Lost over an earlier sleep, see brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3() */
+	if (!pci_device_is_present(devinfo->pdev))
+		return 0;
+
 	brcmf_pcie_fwcon_timer(devinfo, false);
 	brcmf_bus_change_state(bus, BRCMF_BUS_DOWN);
 
@@ -2696,6 +2700,16 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3(struct device *dev)
 	devinfo = bus->bus_priv.pcie->devinfo;
 	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Enter, dev=%p, bus=%p\n", dev, bus);
 
+	/*
+	 * The host bridge could not bring the link back. Any BAR access now
+	 * could stall the CPU, so stay down; with the bus down, firmware
+	 * commands and transmits are refused early.
+	 */
+	if (!pci_device_is_present(devinfo->pdev)) {
+		brcmf_err(bus, "device lost over suspend, staying down\n");
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
 	/* Check if device is still up and running, if so we are ready */
 	if (brcmf_pcie_read_reg32(devinfo, devinfo->reginfo->intmask) != 0) {
 		brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "Try to wakeup device....\n");
